<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Mpororo</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1750 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived pastoral kingdom between Uganda and Rwanda whose breakup left a patchwork of small chiefdoms later absorbed by Ankole.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mpororo arose in the mid-17th century in the grasslands of south-western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/uganda">Uganda</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a>, ruled by the Bashambo clan. Traditions connect its founding with the decline of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ndorwa">Kingdom of Ndorwa</a> and the rivalries of the Kingdom of Rwanda and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Kingdom of Ankole</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-keeping kingdom with a court and royal drums like its neighbours. Its power seems to have rested on the king's herds and on alliances with pastoral clans. Only fragments of its history survive in oral tradition.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the mid-18th century Mpororo split into several small principalities, among them Rujumbura and Kajara. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankole-agreement">Ankole Agreement</a> of 1901 most of these were merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Kingdom of Ankole</a>, while others went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigezi">Kigezi</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1650 CE – 1750 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1750 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Runyankole, Rukiga</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uganda">Uganda</a>, <a href="/countries/rwanda">Rwanda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mpororo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mpororo" aria-label="Kingdom of Mpororo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5601 2111 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Mpororo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5852 2457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5921 2367h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5921 2367h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Uganda. <a href="/atlas?year=1700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mpororo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
